{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538133-which-edition-of-dark-ages-is-your-favourite-and-why","id":1538133,"title":"Which edition of Dark Ages is your favourite and why.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-05T08:56:31-07:00","id":1538133,"title":"Which edition of Dark Ages is your favourite and why.","content":"A chance to climb on your soap box and tell me which edition is your favourite and why. Vampire: the Dark Ages, Dark Ages: Vampire or DAV20.<br /> Pros and cons of each edition, preferred system, preferred setting etc, all welcome.<br /> My motive is simple. I own all three and can\u2019t decide which to use for a new chronicle. Your input will be most appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T10:43:55-07:00","id":1538139,"title":"","content":"For feel and aethetic id go 1st ed and 2nd ed for mechanics and setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T11:45:02-07:00","id":1538140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538133-which-edition-of-dark-ages-is-your-favourite-and-why?p=1538139#post1538139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For feel and aethetic id go 1st ed and 2nd ed for mechanics and setting</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. <br /> Could you give reasons why you suggest those?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T11:53:42-07:00","id":1538141,"title":"","content":"i absolutlely love DAV20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T12:04:50-07:00","id":1538143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538133-which-edition-of-dark-ages-is-your-favourite-and-why?p=1538141#post1538141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i absolutlely love DAV20</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you go into what you love about it compared to the other two editions?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T12:14:10-07:00","id":1538146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andreas Rayne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538133-which-edition-of-dark-ages-is-your-favourite-and-why?p=1538143#post1538143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you go into what you love about it compared to the other two editions?</div> </div> </div> </div>it's imho, darker and less gratuitous in some place,sorry about not giving an in-depth analysis rn I got bit occupied all of sudden","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T14:34:13-07:00","id":1538152,"title":"","content":"We have some of the first edition of Dark Ages VTM and I did like the Order of Bitter Ashes and how I started to like the DA version of the Ventrue clan over there modern counterparts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T17:04:55-07:00","id":1538158,"title":"","content":"The first edition of <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i> remains the most intellectually and aesthetically cohesive. Reading the book there is a lot of material which is more or less a cut and paste from the second edition of <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i>. Nevertheless, it still presents a very strong view of the world of Cainites prior to the Anarch Revolt, and a medieval world in change with the rise of the Tremere, and with conflicts in Eastern Europe and the Mediterranean. It's worthwhile noting that some features of the book, such as including level six Disciplines, Merits and Flaws in the main rulebook, or alternate moralities which are viable for a conventional group of characters, were a departure from established practice at the time, despite how normal they feel now.<br /> <br /> The story goes that Mark Rein-Hagen wanted a vampiric <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</i>, whilst Jennifer Hartshorn, the developer, wanted a more historically accurate game. Hartshorn won out (though some of the prospective material on vampiric roses and fae cattle did appear in <i>The Book of Storyteller's Secrets</i>). I personally think that Hartshorn's focus on gothic horror (she had been the first, and best, developer of <i>Wraith: the Oblivion</i>), and the subsequent development work on the game's supplement's over the following couple of years made the game a success, and is the reason why we are still talking about it now.<br /> <br /> <i>Dark Ages: Vampire</i> is far weaker in theme and aesthetics. One of the aims of Philippe Boule in this edition was clearly to push the game away from its routes in second edition <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i>. The results are, I would argue, somewhat mixed. There are some clear successes, such as the re-imagining of Mortis, or the updating of the Road system into something more detailed and coherent. But the notion of High Clans and Low Clans doesn't really work, nor does the War of Princes (as presented clearly and painfully in <i>Under the Black Cross</i>, the worst chronicle without exception published by White Wolf). There are mechanical interactions which clearly have not been thoroughly considered. For instance, with weapons and combat there was no consideration paid to the addition of overage and division between bashing and lethal damage. The index is terrible (core rules are not referenced, but illustrations of signature characters are), and I am still resentful of the plagiarised map on the opening endpapers. <br /> <br /> The twentieth anniversary edition of <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i> fixed some things, and broke others. Overall, this presents the most functional and robust set of rules, a fairly mixed bag in terms of art (having it all in colour is a bit unforgiving in places), and an indicator that editing and development are important; from page to page you can go from well-written descriptions of the setting and rules, to paragraphs which are barely coherent. Clearly, the underlying quality is solely down to the strength of the original authors, which shows through in the final product. And there are some bizarre design choices - did anyone want the Ahrimanes, or the Niktuku as bloodlines?<br /> <br /> The chapter on Roads is a complete mess, and the weapons table only partly fixed, but then you have some very good guidance for Storytellers. And the book has a chapter on the medieval world which focuses on Italy and Eastern Europe, has multiple factual errors on most pages, and seems to think that places like Hungary are a mystery to players of the game.<br /> <br /> If only there was a good edition, to combine the strengths of the various editions, and to get rid of at least most of the obvious flaws.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T17:42:51-07:00","id":1538159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-i